      "curator_note": "Generic scheme for an unsaturated heteroatom, R-CR=Y(+.) -> R. + RC#Y(+). Book draws 2 arc(s); moves <1,2> are drawn (the odd electron on Y into the C=Y bond, and one electron of the R-C sigma bond into that same bond), move <3> is an implicit homolysis hook required for electron balance (not drawn on the page; R. is simply written as a product). Instantiated by the curator as Y = O with R = CH3 on the sp2 carbon, i.e. the acetone molecular ion n-ionized at oxygen, giving the acetyl (acylium) cation. The page prints no m/z, no intensity and no compound name for this scheme."
